{"voice":"kokoro af_heart","speed":0.92,"pages":{"0":{"text":"Mateo and the Floating Train","src":"p0.mp3","dur":2.52,"t":[[0.26,0.84],[0.84,1.1],[1.1,1.2],[1.2,1.36],[1.36,1.76]]},"1":{"text":"Mateo put his new toy train on the track. He wanted it to cross a big gap between two crates, but there was no bridge! \"How can my train cross without falling?\" Mateo asked. Chike brought over two strong magnets. \"We don't need a bridge,\" Chike smiled. \"We can make the train float!\"","src":"p1.mp3","dur":18.55,"t":[[0.3,0.82],[0.82,1],[1,1.14],[1.14,1.34],[1.34,1.58],[1.58,1.9],[1.9,2.2],[2.2,2.32],[2.32,2.54],[3.22,3.27],[3.24,3.42],[3.42,3.6],[3.6,3.68],[3.68,3.88],[3.88,4.08],[4.08,4.26],[4.26,4.54],[4.54,4.88],[4.88,5.14],[5.14,5.36],[5.36,5.8],[5.8,5.92],[5.92,6.02],[6.02,6.26],[6.26,6.52],[7.16,7.5],[7.5,7.7],[7.7,7.86],[7.86,8.12],[8.12,8.48],[8.48,8.78],[8.78,9.36],[9.76,10.28],[10.28,10.5],[11.44,11.54],[11.54,11.86],[11.86,12.14],[12.14,12.38],[12.38,12.74],[12.74,13.02],[13.88,14.06],[14.06,14.24],[14.24,14.34],[14.34,14.44],[14.44,14.76],[15.2,15.46],[15.46,15.88],[16.58,16.82],[16.82,16.96],[16.96,17.1],[17.1,17.26],[17.26,17.48],[17.48,17.82]]},"3":{"text":"Suddenly, the workshop transformed into a starry canyon! The metallic track began to glow. Mateo placed matching magnets on the bottom of the train and along the track. Because the same sides of magnets push away from each other, the train lifted right into the air! \"It's floating!\" cheered Yuna.","src":"p3.mp3","dur":19.45,"t":[[0,0.6],[0.84,0.96],[0.96,1.22],[1.22,1.88],[1.88,2.4],[2.4,2.56],[2.56,3.02],[3.02,3.26],[4.14,4.19],[4.14,4.36],[4.36,4.8],[4.8,5.18],[5.18,5.44],[5.44,5.68],[6.6,6.88],[6.88,7.08],[7.08,7.46],[7.46,7.92],[7.92,8.4],[8.4,8.48],[8.48,8.78],[8.78,8.94],[8.94,9.04],[9.04,9.28],[9.28,9.76],[9.76,9.98],[9.98,10.26],[10.26,10.5],[11.2,11.32],[11.32,11.58],[11.58,11.82],[11.82,12.14],[12.14,12.38],[12.38,12.66],[12.66,13.1],[13.1,13.38],[13.38,13.6],[13.6,13.72],[13.72,14],[14.32,14.48],[14.48,14.72],[14.72,15.04],[15.04,15.64],[15.64,15.9],[15.9,16.02],[16.02,16.24],[17.04,17.22],[17.22,17.46],[18.12,18.42],[18.42,18.78]]},"5":{"text":"\"This is called maglev,\" Mateo explained. \"Without wheels touching the track, there is much less friction to slow us down!\" Chike flipped a switch to push the train forward with magnetic power. Whoosh! The train glided silently across the canyon gap and landed safely on the other side.","src":"p5.mp3","dur":19.38,"t":[[0.2,0.5],[0.5,0.66],[0.66,0.96],[0.96,1.54],[1.96,2.48],[2.48,2.78],[3.98,4.03],[3.98,4.26],[4.26,4.68],[4.68,4.98],[4.98,5.24],[5.66,5.76],[5.76,5.9],[5.9,6.08],[6.08,6.38],[6.38,6.66],[6.66,7.02],[7.02,7.22],[7.22,7.44],[7.44,7.74],[8.58,8.88],[8.88,9.1],[9.1,9.3],[9.3,9.52],[9.52,9.82],[9.82,9.96],[9.96,10.14],[10.14,10.34],[10.34,10.72],[10.72,11.06],[11.06,11.34],[11.34,11.86],[12.92,13.24],[13.9,13.95],[13.92,14.16],[14.16,14.6],[14.6,15.02],[15.02,15.54],[15.54,15.8],[15.8,16.04],[16.04,16.4],[16.4,16.88],[16.88,17.1],[17.1,17.58],[17.58,18.04],[18.04,18.16],[18.16,18.3],[18.3,18.7]]},"7":{"text":"Click! The magical canyon faded back into the workshop. The toy train settled gently on Mateo’s desk. \"Less friction means more speed!\" Mateo laughed. \"Next time, I'm building a track that goes up the wall!\"","src":"p7.mp3","dur":14.53,"t":[[0.08,0.46],[0.46,0.86],[0.86,1.22],[1.22,1.7],[1.7,2.1],[2.1,2.54],[2.54,2.74],[2.74,2.88],[2.88,3.2],[4.04,4.09],[4.06,4.22],[4.22,4.62],[4.62,4.92],[4.92,5.42],[5.42,5.88],[5.88,6.46],[6.46,6.68],[7.48,7.68],[7.68,7.94],[7.94,8.36],[8.36,8.66],[8.66,9.04],[9.64,10.16],[10.16,10.38],[11.18,11.28],[11.28,11.7],[11.96,12.18],[12.18,12.46],[12.46,12.62],[12.62,12.9],[12.9,13.16],[13.16,13.38],[13.38,13.48],[13.48,13.6],[13.6,13.86]]},"9":{"text":"What Mateo and Chike learned “We didn’t need a bridge,” Mateo said. “We just needed to understand how magnets push.”","src":"p9.mp3","dur":8.2,"t":[[0.18,0.42],[0.42,0.98],[0.98,1.18],[1.18,1.58],[1.58,1.9],[2.46,2.72],[2.72,2.94],[2.94,3.06],[3.06,3.16],[3.16,3.54],[3.88,4.4],[4.4,4.66],[5.02,5.3],[5.3,5.48],[5.48,5.76],[5.76,5.98],[5.98,6.28],[6.28,6.76],[6.76,7],[7,7.5]]},"10":{"text":"3 big takeaways Word to know maglev Maglev is a way to make a train float above its track using magnets, with no wheels touching. Same Sides Push Away Mateo put matching magnets on the bottom of the train and along the track. Because the same sides of magnets push away from each other, the train lifted into the air and floated, with no bridge needed. Less Friction Means More Speed Friction is the rubbing that slows things down, and Mateo's train had much less of it because no wheels touched the track. That is why it crossed the gap so smoothly, and Mateo laughed, \"Less friction means more speed!\" Try it at home: Slowly bring two magnets together, then flip one over and try again: feel when they snap together and when the same sides push apart (never put magnets in your mouth).","src":"p10.mp3","dur":53.03,"t":[[0,0.25],[0.5,0.76],[0.76,1.32],[1.9,2.12],[2.12,2.3],[2.3,2.48],[3,3.54],[4.04,4.6],[4.6,4.8],[4.8,4.9],[4.9,5.06],[5.06,5.24],[5.24,5.36],[5.36,5.48],[5.48,5.7],[5.7,6.06],[6.06,6.4],[6.4,6.6],[6.6,6.88],[6.88,7.28],[7.28,7.64],[7.64,8.3],[8.3,8.52],[8.52,8.82],[8.82,9.2],[10.14,10.3],[10.3,10.72],[10.72,11.08],[11.08,11.42],[12.2,12.62],[12.62,12.82],[12.82,13],[13,13.6],[13.6,13.94],[13.94,14.04],[14.04,14.3],[14.3,14.46],[14.46,14.56],[14.56,14.84],[14.84,15.24],[15.24,15.42],[15.42,15.7],[15.7,15.96],[16.88,17.42],[17.42,17.62],[17.62,17.88],[17.88,18.18],[18.18,18.42],[18.42,18.68],[18.68,19.08],[19.08,19.34],[19.34,19.54],[19.54,19.68],[19.68,19.98],[20.34,20.52],[20.52,20.8],[20.8,21.08],[21.08,21.4],[21.4,21.54],[21.54,21.8],[21.8,22.1],[22.1,22.36],[22.36,23.02],[23.02,23.28],[23.28,23.54],[23.54,23.9],[24.9,24.98],[24.98,25.22],[25.22,25.7],[25.7,26.08],[26.08,26.42],[27.24,27.52],[27.6,27.92],[27.92,28.08],[28.08,28.3],[28.3,28.62],[28.62,28.92],[28.92,29.42],[29.42